# A node's verbs, which used to be the top of its detail.
#
# The screen this replaced opened with thirteen of them: a full panel of actions above the first
# fact about the node, with "Remove from radio" on screen before its battery level, and every
# reading below the fold. So a reader who pressed A on a node to find out *what it was* got a
# menu instead - which is the one thing a detail screen is not.
#
# What to watch is the trade this makes. The detail now opens on the node - one row at the top
# that says "Actions", and Identity and Signal in view under it - and the verbs are one press
# further in, on a screen that says whose they are in its own app bar. Every row there is a
# press, which is why its action bar is three keycaps rather than seven: there is no row on it
# that A means nothing on.
#
# The Nodes list has three rows before its first node - the filter row, the sort row and the
# Map (MESH_UI_NODES_LEAD_ROWS) - so a node's row is its index in the demo roster plus three.
# Alfa Ridge is seeds[1] and row 4; it reports enough to fill the first screen with facts.

scene demo
clock 2026-01-15 12:00
tab nodes
key down 4

# The detail, as it opens. The cursor starts on the Actions row - a card of its own above the
# first heading, which is the one row on this screen that is a control rather than a report.
key a
hold 1600

# Past it, to show what the change bought: Identity and Signal are both on the first screenful
# now, and the cursor on a card of facts takes the focus ring rather than a row highlight.
key right
hold 1400
key right
hold 1400

# Back to the top, and in.
key left
key left
key a
hold 1600

# Down the verbs. The discs keep their families - the accent for an ordinary verb, the warning
# family for ignore, the error family for remove - and the labels stay one colour, which is the
# half of this the old card of eleven accented rows could not say.
key down 6
hold 1200
key down 2
hold 1600

# The remove row arms rather than acting, and the bar drops to two keycaps while it is armed:
# an armed bar says one thing, not four.
key a
hold 1800

# Anything but A stands it down again.
key up
hold 1200

# And B lands back on the detail, on the row this was opened from rather than at the top of a
# hundred-row screen.
key b
hold 1600
